Just out of curiosity, can you recall which stor[y/ies] had them all 
female? I only ask because I've never heard that take on them before and 
now I'm curious. Anyway, just for the heck of it, I desided to see what 
Nethack actually says on the matter. The monster database describes "the 
monstrous mummy of some ancient king" so that one would be male.

But then I rememered something I'd been thinking about before, there's 
no direct way to look at a monster and tell what sex it is. Of course it 
almost never matters, but sometimes I've wondered, like when I'm naming 
a new pet. Well after poking aroudn the source code a bit the easiest 
way to check I found find was to apply a mirror to it. If not effected, 
the monster "ignores his/her/its reflecton". So anyway it turns out 
liches can be either male for female, according to that test. Saddly 
animals are always "it" apperently, so I guess I'll just have to avoid 
names like Lady and Rex for my pets.

